# A thread of the OS server overflows its stack on purpose (roadmap
# memory.md M6, D10's rule; tests/posix/overflow.c): its stack is a segment
# of its own, so the overflow faults (#SS) before it writes anything not its
# own; the root reports it and starts the thread again after the fault,
# where the server's policy ends the process it served (process 3, in entry
# 2: thread 19) and serves the next one in that entry.
program: idle
define: TEST_POSIX_OVERFLOW
define: TEST_OS_OVERFLOW
keys: {wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}
# DOSBox-X checks no stack segment's limit (docs/emulators.md).
emulators: bochs mame
match: contains
timeout: 60
---
rx286: os: thread 19 faulted serving process 3: it is ended
overflow: the child ended by signal 9
overflow: the next child: exit 7
